      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "collection-template"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Collection Template\n\nA collection is a graph that presents other graphs.\n\nA **member** is a graph the collection contains: a Portal node, and a `contains` edge from the collection's members port to it. Anything else in the graph is just a node.\n\nThe Detail, Summary and Glyph are not written by hand: the Method reads the members and writes them. Each tile shows the member graph's own name, description (or its kind) and glyph colour, read when the member is opened, so nothing is copied into the collection. The Detail is a page: it starts at the regular 3:2, stretches with its rows up to a square, then scrolls.\n\nThis template hands on the Method and the Collection class through one export."
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1791502752029,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "collection-template-derive-method",
      "type": "method",
      "label": "Derive the collection views",
      "position": {
        "x": 200,
        "y": 1300
      },
      "width": 420,
      "height": 260,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "call",
          "key": "call",
          "label": "Call",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "event",
          "angle": 180
        },
        {
          "id": "result",
          "key": "result",
          "label": "Result",
          "direction": "output",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 0
        },
        {
          "id": "invokes",
          "key": "invokes",
          "label": "invokes",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "event",
          "angle": 180
        }
      ],
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "call",
          "key": "call",
          "label": "Call",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "event",
          "angle": 180,
          "portId": "call"
        },
        {
          "id": "result",
          "key": "result",
          "label": "Result",
          "direction": "output",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 0,
          "portId": "result"
        },
        {
          "id": "invokes",
          "key": "invokes",
          "label": "invokes",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "event",
          "angle": 180,
          "portId": "invokes"
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "scriptName": "Derive the collection views",
        "parameters": [],
        "effects": [
          {
            "kind": "update-node",
            "targets": [
              "collection-template-detail",
              "collection-template-summary",
              "collection-template-glyph",
              "collection-template-declaration",
              "collection-template-collection",
              "collection-template-icon",
              "collection-template-environment"
            ]
          }
        ],
        "allowMutations": true,
        "dryRun": false,
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "collection-template-declaration"
        },
        "source": "// Derives the collection's views from the graphs it holds: nothing is typed into a summary.\n// A member is a graph the collection holds, and nothing in the collection graph is one unless it was made one. There are two ways:\n//   - a Portal the collection contains (a `contains` edge from its members port);\n//   - a graph in its own folder, when it says so (data.includeFolder), for an address the host can list (github://).\n// The members are the union, without repeats. The member graphs are read through api.readGraph, which returns what the app has already\n// loaded to open them. The Method writes the Detail, the Summary and the Glyph, the size of the Detail and Summary (the Detail stretches\n// with its rows, up to a square), the window that holds them, and a line on the collection saying where its members come from.\nconst clean = (value) => String(value ?? '').trim();\nconst esc = (value) => clean(value)\n  .replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/</g, '&lt;').replace(/>/g, '&gt;').replace(/\"/g, '&quot;').replace(/'/g, '&#39;');\nconst INK = '#7543a4';\nconst MAX_READ = 100;\n\nconst nodes = await api.getNodes();\n// The window takes the Detail's shape, holds every node, and its stage (measured, like the stage numbers, in hundredths of the window's width) holds the cards seen when browsing.\nconst fitWindow = ({ shape, stage, cards, all, pad }) => {\n  const box = (list) => ({ l: Math.min(...list.map((n) => n.position.x)), t: Math.min(...list.map((n) => n.position.y)), r: Math.max(...list.map((n) => n.position.x + n.width)), b: Math.max(...list.map((n) => n.position.y + n.height)) });\n  const A = box(all);\n  const C = box(cards.length ? cards : all);\n  const across = 100 - stage.left - stage.right;\n  const down = 100 * shape - stage.top - stage.bottom;\n  const clamp = (value, low, high) => Math.min(high, Math.max(low, value));\n  let w = Math.ceil(Math.max((C.r - C.l + 2 * pad) * 100 / across, (C.b - C.t + 2 * pad) * 100 / down, A.r - A.l, (A.b - A.t) / shape));\n  for (let tries = 0; ; tries += 1) {\n    const h = Math.round(w * shape);\n    const xLow = Math.ceil(Math.max(A.r - w, C.r + pad - w * (100 - stage.right) / 100));\n    const xHigh = Math.floor(Math.min(A.l, C.l - pad - w * stage.left / 100));\n    const yLow = Math.ceil(Math.max(A.b - h, C.b + pad - (h - w * stage.bottom / 100)));\n    const yHigh = Math.floor(Math.min(A.t, C.t - pad - w * stage.top / 100));\n    if ((xLow <= xHigh && yLow <= yHigh) || tries > 800) {\n      return { x: clamp(Math.round((C.l + C.r - w) / 2), xLow, xHigh), y: clamp(Math.round((C.t + C.b) / 2 - w * (stage.top + down / 2) / 100), yLow, yHigh), width: w, height: h };\n    }\n    w = Math.ceil(w * 1.01) + 1;\n  }\n};\n// A graph that borrows this Method from its template declares its own writes. The newer surfaces (the Icon and, where the template did not write one before, the\n// environment) are written only where that declaration names them, so an older graph keeps what it has and is not refused.\nconst declaredHere = (target) => Boolean(target) && nodes.some((method) => method.type === 'method' && (method.data?.effects || []).some((effect) => effect.kind === 'update-node' && (!effect.targets || effect.targets.includes(target.id))));\nconst edges = await api.getEdges();\nconst byId = new Map(nodes.map((node) => [node.id, node]));\nconst root = nodes.find((node) => clean(node.type) === 'root');\nconst collection = nodes.find((node) => clean(node.type) === 'collection');\nconst title = clean(collection?.data?.title || collection?.label) || 'Collection';\nconst sort = ['name', 'kind', 'newest'].includes(clean(collection?.data?.sort)) ? clean(collection.data.sort) : 'order';\n// What the Summary shows: the members' names (the default), or the first member's own card, so a collection ordered newest first shows its newest member.\nconst summaryFrom = clean(collection?.data?.summaryFrom) === 'first' ? 'first' : 'members';\n\nconst keyOf = (address) => clean(address).replace(/#.*$/, '').replace(/^https?:\\/\\/twilite\\.zone\\//i, 'tlz://twilite.zone/');\n\n// The portals the collection contains, in the order of their edges.\nconst portals = edges\n  .filter((edge) => clean(edge.type) === 'contains' && collection && edge.source === collection.id)\n  .map((edge) => byId.get(edge.target))\n  .filter((node) => node && clean(node.type) === 'portal');\nconst refOf = (portal) => clean(portal.data?.target?.ref || portal.data?.sourceRef || portal.data?.ref);\n\n// The folder: the graphs one level below the folder this collection's own root sits in, for a collection the host can list.\nconst includeFolder = collection?.data?.includeFolder === true;\nlet folderAddresses = [];\nlet folderNote = '';\nif (includeFolder) {\n  const own = clean(root?.data?.document?.url);\n  const where = /^github:\\/\\/([^/]+)\\/([^/]+)\\/(?:(.*)\\/)?[^/]+$/.exec(own);\n  if (!where) {\n    folderNote = /^(tlz|https?):/i.test(own) ? 'a published site cannot list its folders' : 'this graph has no github:// address to list';\n  } else {\n    const [, owner, repository, directory = ''] = where;\n    try {\n      const entries = await api.listRepositoryDirectory({ repo: `${owner}/${repository}`, path: directory, branch: 'main' });\n      folderAddresses = entries.filter((entry) => clean(entry.type) === 'dir' && clean(entry.name))\n        .sort((a, b) => clean(a.name).localeCompare(clean(b.name)))\n        .map((entry) => `github://${owner}/${repository}/${[directory, clean(entry.name)].filter(Boolean).join('/')}/root.node`);\n    } catch (error) { folderNote = `the folder could not be listed (${clean(error?.message) || 'no reason given'})`; }\n  }\n}\n\n// The union, without repeats: the portals in their order, then the folder.\nconst entries = [];\nconst seen = new Set();\nconst add = (address, from, portal = null) => {\n  const key = keyOf(address) || `portal:${portal?.id}`;\n  if (seen.has(key)) return;\n  seen.add(key);\n  entries.push({ address, from, portal });\n};\nportals.forEach((portal) => add(refOf(portal), 'portal', portal));\nfolderAddresses.forEach((address) => add(address, 'folder'));\n\nconst kindWords = (kind) => { const words = clean(kind).replace(/-/g, ' '); return words ? words[0].toUpperCase() + words.slice(1) : 'Graph'; };\nconst slugOf = (address) => { const parts = clean(address).replace(/#.*$/, '').split('/').filter(Boolean); const last = parts[parts.length - 1] || ''; return /\\.node$/.test(last) && parts.length > 1 ? parts[parts.length - 2] : last; };\n\n// What a tile says about a member comes from the member itself: its name, its description (or its kind when it has none) and the\n// colour of its own glyph. Only the first MAX_READ are read, so a large folder does not read every graph in it; the rest show their\n// folder's name. A graph found in the folder that cannot be read is not a graph, and is left out.\n// A member's own Summary view: the face of its Surface chain whose level is summary, when it holds plain html (no template syntax, no scripts).\nconst summaryOf = (graph, rootNode) => {\n  const links = Array.isArray(graph.edges) ? graph.edges : [];\n  const faceById = new Map(graph.nodes.filter((node) => clean(node.type) === 'face').map((node) => [node.id, node]));\n  const chain = [];\n  let at = faceById.get(links.find((edge) => clean(edge.type) === 'surface' && edge.source === rootNode.id)?.target);\n  while (at && chain.length < 8 && !chain.includes(at)) { chain.push(at); at = faceById.get(links.find((edge) => clean(edge.type) === 'next-face' && edge.source === at.id)?.target); }\n  const face = chain.find((node) => clean(node.data?.semanticLevel) === 'summary');\n  const html = face?.data?.content?.kind === 'html' ? String(face.data.content.value || '') : '';\n  return html && !/\\{\\{|<script/i.test(html) ? html : '';\n};\nconst factsOf = async (entry, index) => {\n  let graph = null;\n  if (entry.address && index < MAX_READ) { try { graph = await api.readGraph(entry.address); } catch (error) { graph = null; } }\n  const found = Array.isArray(graph?.nodes);\n  const items = found ? graph.nodes : [];\n  const rootNode = items.find((node) => clean(node.type) === 'root');\n  const glyph = items.find((node) => clean(node.type) === 'glyph')?.data?.glyph;\n  const name = clean(rootNode?.data?.identity?.name) || clean(entry.portal?.label) || slugOf(entry.address) || entry.address;\n  const kind = kindWords(rootNode?.data?.intent?.kind);\n  const lift = found && rootNode ? summaryOf(graph, rootNode) : '';\n  return { lift, ref: entry.address, from: entry.from, dropped: entry.from === 'folder' && index < MAX_READ && !found, name, kind,\n    description: clean(rootNode?.data?.identity?.description) || kind, date: clean(rootNode?.data?.identity?.releaseDate), tint: /^#[0-9a-f]{6}$/i.test(clean(glyph?.color)) ? clean(glyph.color) : INK };\n};\nlet members = (await Promise.all(entries.map(factsOf))).filter((member) => !member.dropped);\nif (sort === 'name') members = [...members].sort((a, b) => a.name.localeCompare(b.name));\n// newest: the dated members first, the latest date first; a member with no date follows, in the order it was listed (the sort is stable)\nif (sort === 'newest') members = [...members].sort((a, b) => (a.date && b.date ? (a.date < b.date ? 1 : (a.date > b.date ? -1 : 0)) : (a.date ? -1 : (b.date ? 1 : 0))));\nif (sort === 'kind') members = [...members].sort((a, b) => a.kind.localeCompare(b.kind) || a.name.localeCompare(b.name));\nconst count = members.length;\nconst countText = `${count} ${count === 1 ? 'graph' : 'graphs'}`;\n\n// Where the members come from, for the collection's editor to show.\nconst fromFolder = members.filter((member) => member.from === 'folder').length;\nconst sources = [\n  portals.length ? `${portals.length} portal${portals.length === 1 ? '' : 's'}` : '',\n  includeFolder && !folderNote ? `${fromFolder} in the folder` : '',\n  `${count} member${count === 1 ? '' : 's'}`\n].filter(Boolean).join(' · ');\nconst problems = [folderNote ? `folder: ${folderNote}` : ''].filter(Boolean);\nconst sourcesLine = problems.length ? `${sources} (${problems.join('; ')})` : sources;\nif (collection && clean(collection.data?.sourcesSummary) !== sourcesLine) await api.updateNode(collection.id, { data: { ...collection.data, sourcesSummary: sourcesLine } });\n\n// The Detail is 100cqw wide. Tiles are 26.2cqw or wider (110px at the regular 420px width), never fewer than two to a row. It starts at\n// the regular 3:2 and stretches with its rows up to a square; beyond that the tile area scrolls.\nconst TILE = 14.2; const GAP = 1.4; const MIN_TILE = 26.2; const PAD = 4; const HEAD = 12;\nconst columns = Math.max(2, Math.floor((100 - 2 * PAD + GAP) / (MIN_TILE + GAP)));\nconst rows = Math.ceil(count / columns);\nconst need = 2 * PAD + HEAD + (rows ? rows * (TILE + GAP) : 22);\nconst ratio = Math.min(1, Math.max(2 / 3, need / 100));\nconst DETAIL_WIDTH = 600; const SUMMARY_WIDTH = 480;\n\nconst frame = (inner, style) => `<div style='container-type:inline-size;width:100%;height:100%'><div style='box-sizing:border-box;width:100%;height:100%;font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,Segoe UI,sans-serif;${style}'>${inner}</div></div>`;\nconst tile = (member) => `<a href='${esc(member.ref)}' style='display:flex;gap:2.2cqw;align-items:flex-start;box-sizing:border-box;height:${TILE}cqw;padding:1.6cqw 2.1cqw;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:1.2cqw;background:#f4edf9;border-left:.65cqw solid ${member.tint};text-decoration:none;color:inherit;min-width:0;overflow:hidden'>`\n  + `<span style='flex:none;width:6.2cqw;height:6.2cqw;border-radius:1.6cqw;background:${member.tint}22;color:${member.tint};display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:600;font-size:3cqw'>${esc(member.name.slice(0, 1).toUpperCase())}</span>`\n  + `<span style='min-width:0'><span style='display:block;font-weight:800;font-size:3.3cqw;line-height:1.25;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:#0f172a'>${esc(member.name)}</span>`\n  + `<span style='display:-webkit-box;-webkit-line-clamp:2;-webkit-box-orient:vertical;overflow:hidden;font-size:2.6cqw;line-height:1.3;color:#64748b'>${esc(member.description)}</span></span></a>`;\nconst body = count\n  ? `<div style='display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(${MIN_TILE}cqw,1fr));gap:${GAP}cqw;align-content:start'>${members.map(tile).join('')}</div>`\n  : `<div style='display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:1.4cqw;min-height:26cqw;border:1px dashed #cbd5e1;border-radius:2.4cqw;color:#64748b;font-size:2.8cqw;text-align:center;padding:2cqw'><span style='font-size:5.4cqw;line-height:1'>+</span>Nothing here yet. Add a graph with a portal.</div>`;\nconst detail = frame(\n  `<div style='display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline;gap:2cqw'><div style='min-width:0'><div style='font-size:2.2cqw;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:${INK}'>Collection</div><div style='font-weight:600;font-size:4cqw;line-height:1.2;color:#0f172a;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis'>${esc(title)}</div></div><div style='font-size:2.2cqw;color:#64748b;white-space:nowrap'>${countText}</div></div>`\n  + `<div style='flex:1;min-height:0;overflow:auto'>${body}</div>`,\n  `padding:${PAD}cqw;border-radius:1cqw;background:#f4edf9;border-top:1.2cqw solid ${INK};display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2cqw`\n);\n// The shelf: the members' own Summary views at one fixed size, in a row that scrolls. Its scrollbar is the plank, and it is visible: the app lets the\n// wheel and a press scroll only what has a scrollbar under the pointer, so a shelf with none could not be scrolled at all. Each stands in a box that is its own container, so what it\n// draws in its own units is drawn at the size of its box. A click on a member goes to it. A member with no Summary of its own is a plain card.\n// The Summary is read from far away, so it is a few big words and not a picture of the members: the kind of thing it is, its name, one line of facts, and the members' names as chips that open them.\n// Nothing here is under 6cqw and all of it is bold (scripts/library/auditSummaryType.mjs measures this). The title and the facts never shrink; the chips give way when the tile is short.\nconst MAX_CHIPS = 5;\nconst chipStyle = (tint) => `box-sizing:border-box;max-width:100%;padding:1.2cqw 3cqw;border-radius:9cqw;background:${tint}1a;border:.5cqw solid ${tint}66;color:#0f172a;font:700 6cqw/1.25 system-ui,-apple-system,Segoe UI,sans-serif;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis`;\nconst chip = (member) => `<a href='${esc(member.ref)}' title='${esc(member.name)}' aria-label='${esc(member.name)}' style='${chipStyle(member.tint)}'>${esc(member.name)}</a>`;\nconst over = count > MAX_CHIPS;\nconst moreChip = over ? `<span style='padding:1.2cqw 3cqw;font:700 6cqw/1.25 system-ui,sans-serif;color:#475569;white-space:nowrap'>+${count - (MAX_CHIPS - 1)} more</span>` : '';\nconst chips = count ? members.slice(0, over ? MAX_CHIPS - 1 : count).map(chip).join('') + moreChip : `<span style='font:700 6cqw/1.3 system-ui,sans-serif;color:#475569'>Nothing here yet. Add a graph with a portal.</span>`;\nconst titleChars = [...String(title)].length;\nconst titleSize = titleChars <= 11 ? 15 : titleChars <= 16 ? 11 : 8.5;\nconst summary = frame(\n  `<div style='flex:none;font:700 6cqw/1.1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:${INK}'>Collection</div>`\n  + `<div style='flex:none;font:850 ${titleSize}cqw/1.02 system-ui,-apple-system,Segoe UI,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.01em;color:#0f172a;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis'>${esc(title)}</div>`\n  + `<div style='flex:none;font:700 6.5cqw/1.2 system-ui,sans-serif;color:#334155'>${countText}</div>`\n  + `<div style='flex:1 1 0;min-height:0;overflow:hidden;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:2cqw;align-content:flex-start'>${chips}</div>`,\n  `padding:4cqw;border-radius:1cqw;background:#f4edf9;border:.8cqw solid ${INK};display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:3cqw;overflow:hidden`\n);\n\nconst icon = `<div style=\"container-type:inline-size;width:100%;height:100%\"><div style=\"box-sizing:border-box;height:100%;background:#7543a4;color:white;display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding:3cqw 4cqw;font-family:system-ui;overflow:hidden\"><div style=\"flex:1;min-height:0;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center\"><div style=\"width:37cqw;height:100%;max-height:37cqw\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" viewBox=\"0 0 120 128\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\"><path d=\"M14 16H106V42H14ZM14 48H106V74H14ZM14 80H106V106H14Z\" fill=\"#fff\"/><path d=\"M24 29H44M24 61H60M24 93H76\" stroke=\"#7543a4\" stroke-width=\"6\"/></svg></div></div><div style=\"background:#42245f;padding:2.5cqw 3cqw;margin:0 -4cqw -3cqw\"><div style=\"font:800 3.8cqw/1.1 system-ui;color:#e0c9f5;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase\">Collection</div><div style=\"font:850 10cqw/1.03 system-ui;letter-spacing:-.04em;overflow-wrap:anywhere;display:-webkit-box;-webkit-line-clamp:2;-webkit-box-orient:vertical;overflow:hidden\">${esc(title)}</div></div></div></div>`;\nconst faces = nodes.filter((node) => clean(node.type) === 'face');\nconst faceFor = (level) => faces.find((node) => clean(node.data?.semanticLevel) === level);\nconst glyph = nodes.find((node) => clean(node.type) === 'glyph');\nconst detailFace = faceFor('detail');\nconst summaryFace = faceFor('summary');\nconst iconFace = faceFor('icon');\n// With an Icon under it the Summary has to be well under the Detail's width, or the Detail takes over before the Summary is ever shown. A graph without one keeps the wider Summary.\nconst ICON_WIDTH = 180;\nconst summaryWidth = declaredHere(iconFace) ? 300 : SUMMARY_WIDTH;\nconst size = (face, width) => ({ width, height: Math.round(width * ratio) });\nif (detailFace) {\n  await api.updateView(detailFace.id, { content: { kind: 'html', value: detail }, view: { ...(detailFace.data?.view || {}), scroll: 'page' } });\n  await api.updateNode(detailFace.id, size(detailFace, DETAIL_WIDTH));\n}\nif (summaryFace) {\n  // the first member's own card, when it has one and the collection asks for it; otherwise the members' names\n  await api.updateView(summaryFace.id, { content: { kind: 'html', value: summaryFrom === 'first' && members[0]?.lift ? members[0].lift : summary } });\n  await api.updateNode(summaryFace.id, size(summaryFace, summaryWidth));\n}\nif (declaredHere(iconFace)) {\n  await api.updateView(iconFace.id, { content: { kind: 'html', value: icon } });\n  await api.updateNode(iconFace.id, size(iconFace, ICON_WIDTH));\n}\nif (glyph) await api.updateNode(glyph.id,{data:{...glyph.data,glyph:{\"kind\":\"svg\",\"value\":\"<svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 120 120\\\"><path d=\\\"M14 16H106V42H14ZM14 48H106V74H14ZM14 80H106V106H14Z\\\" fill=\\\"#fff\\\"/></svg>\",\"color\":\"#7543a4\"}}});\n\n// Collection environment: a furnished archive, with an unobstructed stage for its members.\nconst envFace = faces.find(node => clean(node.data?.view?.payload) === 'node.web.environment');\nconst editorOnly = new Set(['root','face','glyph','import','export','method','script']);\nconst shown = nodes.filter(node => node.position && node.visible !== false && !editorOnly.has(clean(node.type)));\nif (root && declaredHere(envFace)) {\n  // The environment surrounds the stage. Its dimensions and stage percentages use the same units.\n  const stageX = 5, stageW = 90, header = 25, footer = 9;\n  const stageH = 100 * ratio - header - footer;\n  const sized = nodes.filter((node) => node.position).map((node) => (node === detailFace ? { ...node, ...size(node, DETAIL_WIDTH) } : node === summaryFace ? { ...node, ...size(node, summaryWidth) } : node === iconFace && declaredHere(iconFace) ? { ...node, ...size(node, ICON_WIDTH) } : node));\n  const pad = 80;\n  const placedWindow = fitWindow({ shape: ratio, stage: { left: stageX, right: 100 - stageX - stageW, top: header, bottom: footer }, cards: shown, all: sized, pad });\n  const { x: x0, y: y0, width: w, height: h } = placedWindow;\n  const titleSize = [...title].length <= 12 ? 9 : [...title].length <= 22 ? 6.6 : 5;\n  const description = clean(collection?.data?.body) || 'A place for things that belong together.';\n  const archive = '<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" viewBox=\"0 0 190 150\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\"><path d=\"M18 120 94 81 177 120 100 145Z\" fill=\"#261637\"/><path d=\"M36 37 110 8 157 31 83 62Z\" fill=\"#d6b8f4\"/><path d=\"M36 37 83 62V130L36 105Z\" fill=\"#65418a\"/><path d=\"M83 62 157 31V99L83 130Z\" fill=\"#a77bd0\"/><path d=\"M89 66 150 40V56L89 82Z M89 88 150 62V78L89 104Z M89 110 150 84V95L89 120Z\" fill=\"#43265f\"/><path d=\"M98 67 111 62M98 89 119 80M98 111 129 98\" stroke=\"#f1d3a5\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"square\"/><path d=\"M42 43 76 61V78L42 60Z M42 66 76 84V101L42 83Z M42 89 76 107V117L42 99Z\" fill=\"#51316f\"/></svg>';\n  const links = members.filter(member=>clean(member.ref)).slice(0,4).map(member=>`<a href='${esc(member.ref)}' style='min-width:0;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:#f5e9ff;text-decoration:none;font-weight:750'>${esc(member.name)} →</a>`).join('');\n  const page = `<div style='container-type:inline-size;width:100%;height:100%'><div style='position:relative;box-sizing:border-box;width:100%;height:100%;overflow:hidden;background:#241533;color:#fff;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif'>`\n    + `<div style='position:absolute;inset:0;background:radial-gradient(ellipse at 85% 10%,#644284 0%,transparent 54%),linear-gradient(145deg,#42245f,#251633 75%)'></div>`\n    + `<div style='position:absolute;inset:0;opacity:.23;background-image:linear-gradient(90deg,transparent 95%,#c5a3e4 96%),linear-gradient(transparent 95%,#c5a3e4 96%);background-size:12cqw 12cqw'></div>`\n    + `<div style='position:absolute;left:5cqw;right:5cqw;top:2.5cqw;height:.45cqw;background:#d6b8f4'></div>`\n    + `<div style='position:absolute;left:5cqw;top:4.1cqw;color:#d6b8f4;font:800 2cqw/1.1 system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em'>COLLECTION / ARCHIVE</div>`\n    + `<div style='position:absolute;left:5cqw;right:28cqw;top:7cqw;font:850 ${titleSize}cqw/1 system-ui;letter-spacing:-.045em;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis'>${esc(title)}</div>`\n    + `<div style='position:absolute;left:5cqw;right:28cqw;top:17.5cqw;font:500 2.6cqw/1.2 system-ui;color:#f1e6fc;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis'>${esc(description)}</div>`\n    + `<div style='position:absolute;left:5cqw;top:21cqw;font:800 2cqw/1 system-ui;color:#f1d3a5;letter-spacing:.05em'>${esc(countText)}</div>`\n    + `<div style='position:absolute;right:5cqw;top:3.5cqw;width:21cqw;height:19cqw'>${archive}</div>`\n    + `<div style='position:absolute;left:5cqw;top:25cqw;width:90cqw;height:${stageH}cqw;box-sizing:border-box;background:#322047;border:.3cqw solid #a889c4;border-top:.75cqw solid #9d78c0;border-radius:1cqw;box-shadow:inset 0 1cqw 2cqw #20142f;background-image:linear-gradient(#b99bd514 .08cqw,transparent .08cqw),linear-gradient(90deg,#b99bd514 .08cqw,transparent .08cqw);background-size:3cqw 3cqw'></div>`\n    + `<div style='position:absolute;left:5cqw;right:5cqw;bottom:6cqw;border-top:.35cqw solid #9d78c0'></div>`\n    + `<div style='position:absolute;left:5cqw;right:5cqw;bottom:2.2cqw;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:3cqw;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;font:700 1.8cqw/1.2 system-ui;color:#d6b8f4'><span style='flex:none;color:#f1d3a5;letter-spacing:.12em'>DIRECTORY</span>${links || '<span>No members yet</span>'}</div></div></div>`;\n  await api.updateView(envFace.id,{content:{kind:'html',value:page},view:{...envFace.data.view,fit:'window',stage:{left:stageX,right:100-stageX-stageW,top:header,bottom:footer}}});\n  await api.updateNode(root.id,{data:{...root.data,membrane:{...root.data?.membrane,bounds:{x:x0,y:y0,width:w,height:h}}}});\n} else if (root) {\n  // Otherwise the window is sized as before.\n  // The window is the Detail's shape and holds everything the graph has.\n  const placed = nodes.filter((node) => node.position).map((node) => (node === detailFace ? { ...node, ...size(node, DETAIL_WIDTH) } : node === summaryFace ? { ...node, ...size(node, summaryWidth) } : node));\n  const pad = 80;\n  let x0 = Math.min(...placed.map((node) => node.position.x)) - pad;\n  let y0 = Math.min(...placed.map((node) => node.position.y)) - pad;\n  let w = Math.max(...placed.map((node) => node.position.x + node.width)) + pad - x0;\n  let h = Math.max(...placed.map((node) => node.position.y + node.height)) + pad - y0;\n  if (w / h < 1 / ratio) { const next = Math.round(h / ratio); x0 -= Math.round((next - w) / 2); w = next; } else { const next = Math.round(w * ratio); y0 -= Math.round((next - h) / 2); h = next; }\n  await api.updateNode(root.id, { data: { ...root.data, membrane: { ...(root.data?.membrane || {}), bounds: { x: Math.round(x0), y: Math.round(y0), width: w, height: h } } } });\n}\nreturn { members:count, columns, rows, ratio:Math.round(ratio*1000)/1000 };\n"
      }
    },
